ibility of any Member of  Parliament is to represent their  constituents I mean you've had a second  job in the past as we know is it  possible for MPS to have second jobs as  well as be an MP I think what we need to  do is actually have rules that the  public can have trust in when I came  into Parliament I had a couple of  non-executive directorships and I gave a  commitment to the 2019 election that  would bring them to close but of course  these were things it didn't have any  interference at all in the job that I  did there was a full-time member to  Parliament but I've chosen that I would  not do that but we need to make sure  that the public can have confidence in  the way that MPS are going around the  business and the primary responsibility  is to represent their concessions and  there are no conflicts of interest  because that's important  why is it the SMP you think that is  taking the lead on this overhaul and not  say labor well I think this has to be an  across party issue because all of us  have a responsibility and I would appeal  to parliamentarians Across the house  let's make sure that we take appropriate  action we need to be sure that we can be  judged by the things that we do in my  plea to colleagues like make sure that  we clean up politics you know we've got  the situation you're talking about  second jobs but there's all sorts of  issues around all party parliamentary  groups that's been raised as well the  fact that there's dark money involved in  many cases too we can't have this so we  need to make sure that we look at all  the mechanisms look at the way the  parliament operates let's make sure that  Parliament is above suspicion and that  we can all take pride and how we go  about the jobs I mean it's just that  we've brought all of this with shortest  media together in one place with an easy  to use tool I mean why has something not  been done before now well I think people  have actually raised this I mean you've  had situations over 