d been a coup to unseat you how do you  feel about it okay I'm actually really  looking forward to the job that I've got  now I spent five and a half years as the  SNP Westminster leader I think I had  four Prime Ministers over that period  I've accepted and Euro was the first  Minister's business Ambassador and I'm  getting on with that job I'm also  commissioning a report in a green  industrial future for Scotland which I'm  going to take six months to do so I'm  really looking forward to the rules that  I'm going to be fulfilling and of course  continuing to work as a as a  constituency MP so it's a a new  departure for me using my previous  skills working in business working in  the city to make sure I can Shine the  Light on the future for Scott was it a  coup though look at the end of the day I  took I took the decision to to stand  down we have an annual election for the  the SNP leader I'd been Consulting with  the first Minister about the ways I can  strengthen the argument for Scottish  independence I'm really pleased about  the job that I'm going to be doing I'm  getting on with that making sure I'm  serving my constituents but I want to  make sure that I'm delivering the the  message is how we can Revitalize the  Scottish economy how we can deliver  sustainable economic growth in fact I've  now got the freedom to do that and I  look forward to having those discussions  with you and others over the course of  the coming months well your ultimate  leader is meeting our prime minister  later on today he's heading up to  Scotland does that show that he's  serious about the Union  you know I think there are differences  that of course that we have with with  Rishi sunak but there are times that we  have to work together there are  important things that the first Minister  and the Prime Minister have to discuss  but my message to Rishi is he has to  respect democracy and he has to respect  that there is a mandate for an  independence referendum that the  Scott